Apache Hardening Service Security:
````````````````````````````````````
1) Hide Apache Version and OS Information:
```````````````````````````````````````````
# vim /etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf

ServerTokens Prod
ServerSignature Off

NOTE: ServerSignature will remove the version information from the page generated
like 403, 404, 502 etc...

# systemctl restart httpd
+++++++++++++++++++++++
If we want to remove information about PHP, we have to edit the php.ini configuration file. The directive should be changed from:

expose_php = On

to:

expose_php = Off




2) Disable Directory Listing:
``````````````````````````````
<Directory /home/sniper/public_html/lol>
	Options -Indexes
</Directory>










3) Restrict Access to Sensitive Directories:
`````````````````````````````````````````````
<VirtualHost *:80>
    ServerName example.com
    DocumentRoot /var/www/html

    # Other virtual host settings

    <Directory /var/www/html/sensitive_directory>
        Require all denied
    </Directory>
</VirtualHost>

